# --- Unity Folders to Ignore ---
[Ll]ibrary/
[Tt]emp/
[Oo]bj/
[Bb]uild/
[Bb]uilds/
[Ll]ogs/
[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/
[Uu]i[Ee]lements[Ss]chema/
MemoryCaptures/
Packages/com.unity.asset-store-tools/
Assets/Packages/

# --- Standard C# / IDE Ignore ---
*.csproj
*.sln
*.suo
*.user
*.userprefs
*.pidb
*.booproj
*.svd
*.unityproj
*.csproj.user
*.designer.cs
*.cache
*.manifest
*.tmp
*.log
.vs/
.idea/
.gradle/
ExportedObj/
.vsconfig

# --- Keep Meta Files ---
# Never ignore meta files; they are the glue of Unity
!*.meta

# --- DLL Handling ---
# Only ignore DLLs if they are in specific "Build" or "Temp" folders.
# If you have DLLs in Assets/, you likely want to track them.
# *.dll (REMOVED: better to track these if they are in Assets)

# Project specific
# CRIT/*
# CUTS/*
# DATA/*
# SOUND/*
LargeObjectPNGs/*
ObjectPNGs/*
Conversations/*
Critters/*